<title>JAPAN: Tunisia Central Bank raises samurai volume--Nikko.</title>
<headline>Tunisia Central Bank raises samurai volume--Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bank of Tunisia increased the issued volume of its 20-year 4.35 percent samurai bonds to 12.5 billion yen from 10 billion yen, lead manager Nikko Securities said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The central bank originally launched 10 billion yen worth of the samurai bonds on July 31.</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Central Bank of Tunisia</p>
<p> AMT		 12.5 bln yen (up from 10 bln yen)</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.35 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  15 Aug 2017</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  15 Aug 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Aug 7 to Aug 11</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P BBB-, Moody's Baa3</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nikko Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Nippon Credit Bank</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
